<title>USA: Pinkerton acquires New York security firm.</title>
<headline>Pinkerton acquires New York security firm.</headline>
<dateline>ENCINO, Calif. 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pinkerton's Inc on Tuesday said it has acquired Signacon Controls Inc, a New York-based integrator of security systems.</p>
<p>Terms of the deal were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Signacon estimates its 1996 revenues at $6.8 million.</p>
<p>Established in 1965, it has 50 employees and is headquartered in Westchester County, north of New York City, with offices in Albany, Buffalo, Rochester and Syracuse.</p>
<p>The company services clients in Connecticut, Massachusetts, New Jersey and New York.</p>
</text>
